  {
    "insert": "\nThe exposé explores the potential of Large Language Models (LLMs) to create personalized learning pathways based on self-set goals, addressing declining lifelong learning participation. It aims to evaluate the suitability of various models, the optimal granularity of learning steps, and the accuracy of time estimations for achieving learning objectives. A mixed-methods approach, involving case studies, benchmarks, and participant evaluations, will assess how well LLMs can guide learners toward meaningful and self-directed educational outcomes.\n"
  },
